      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 2 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Southwest Monsoon (Habagat)\nIssued at: 2:00 AM, 03 July 2025(Thursday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Metro Manila, Bataan, Rizal(San Mateo, Rodriguez), Bulacan(San Jose del Monte, Norzagaray, Marilao, Meycauayan, Obando) and Cavite(Ternate, Naic, Tanza, Rosario, Noveleta, Cavite City, Bacoor, Maragondon, General Trias, Kawit, Imus).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate with occasional heavy rains over Laguna, Quezon, Nueva Ecija and Tarlac within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Zambales, Pampanga, Batangas, Cavite(Alfonso, Amadeo, General Emilio Aguinaldo, Indang, Magallanes, Mendez, Silang, Tagaytay, Trece Martires, Carmona, Dasmarinas, Gen. Mariano Alvarez), Rizal(Antipolo, Tanay, Angono, Baras, Binangonan, Cainta, Cardona, Jala-Jala, Morong, Pililla, Taytay, Teresa) and Bulacan(Angat, Balagtas, Baliuag, Bocaue, Bulakan, Bustos, Calumpit, Malolos, Dona Remedios Trinidad, Guiguinto, Hagonoy, Pandi, Paombong, Plaridel, Pulilan, San Ildefonso, San Miguel, San Rafael, Santa Maria) which may persist within 3 hours.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 5:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
